WEBVTT

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:04.751
That's very good.

00:00:08.926 --> 00:00:10.393
Well, that's very nice.

00:00:10.427 --> 00:00:12.122
No, it isn't.

00:00:12.162 --> 00:00:14.892
I just can't get it right.

00:00:14.998 --> 00:00:17.159
You think the wings
are too big?

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.224
Oh, no, not at all.

00:00:18.268 --> 00:00:20.668
Birds have wings of all sizes,
Eric.

00:00:20.704 --> 00:00:24.435
And you shouldn't worry
about making it look perfect.

00:00:24.474 --> 00:00:28.069
But Mrs. Narsu said we should
try to make our sculptures

00:00:28.111 --> 00:00:29.738
as realistic as possible.

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:30.838
Well, she's right.

00:00:30.881 --> 00:00:32.644
It is important that you be able

00:00:32.683 --> 00:00:35.550
to make the clay take the shape
you want it to have

00:00:35.585 --> 00:00:37.917
but you're not supposed
to be concentrating

00:00:37.988 --> 00:00:39.114
on technique today.

00:00:39.156 --> 00:00:40.680
I'm here to help you focus

00:00:40.724 --> 00:00:43.921
on the feelings you want
to convey with your sculpture.

00:00:43.961 --> 00:00:46.259
For instance

00:00:46.296 --> 00:00:49.060
what do you think about
when you see a bird?

00:00:49.099 --> 00:00:50.657
Flying?

00:00:50.701 --> 00:00:52.032
Fine.

00:00:52.069 --> 00:00:56.472
So make your sculpture
make me think of flying, too.

00:01:04.581 --> 00:01:06.048
How's it going, Data?

00:01:06.083 --> 00:01:07.675
I have finished.

00:01:07.718 --> 00:01:11.119
The dimensions are accurate
to within 1.3%.

00:01:11.154 --> 00:01:13.884
I'm sure they are.

00:01:13.924 --> 00:01:18.258
Data, you obviously don't have
a problem with realism

00:01:18.295 --> 00:01:20.320
but you're here to work
on your imagination.

00:01:20.364 --> 00:01:21.991
Maybe you should try

00:01:22.032 --> 00:01:24.865
something a little more...
abstract.

00:01:24.901 --> 00:01:26.562
Here...

00:01:26.603 --> 00:01:31.404
I want you to start a new piece.

00:01:31.441 --> 00:01:36.777
I'd like you to sculpt... music.

00:01:36.813 --> 00:01:41.580
Counselor, music is a collection
of acoustic vibrations.

00:01:41.618 --> 00:01:44.815
How can I reproduce a sound
with clay?

00:01:44.855 --> 00:01:48.723
Well, think of the effects
that sounds have on people.

00:01:48.759 --> 00:01:52.024
The images that music
brings to your mind.

00:01:52.062 --> 00:01:53.962
And then, give it a form.

00:02:12.716 --> 00:02:14.581
It's a start.

00:02:16.286 --> 00:02:19.414
Riker to Data,
please report to the Bridge.

00:02:19.456 --> 00:02:20.753
Acknowledged, sir.

00:02:20.791 --> 00:02:22.122
On my way.

00:02:22.159 --> 00:02:25.720
Captain's Log, Stardate 47615.2.

00:02:25.762 --> 00:02:31.132
We have encountered
a rogue comet in Sector 1156.

00:02:31.168 --> 00:02:34.103
It is not native
to this region of space

00:02:34.137 --> 00:02:36.162
and there is no previous record
of this object

00:02:36.206 --> 00:02:37.468
on any Federation charts.

00:02:37.507 --> 00:02:39.498
Based on its present trajectory

00:02:39.543 --> 00:02:41.909
the comet appears
to have originated

00:02:41.945 --> 00:02:43.412
in the D'Arsay system.

00:02:43.447 --> 00:02:45.074
That's over two sectors away.

00:02:45.115 --> 00:02:46.446
That is correct, sir.

00:02:46.483 --> 00:02:49.680
This object has been en route
for 87 million years.

00:02:49.719 --> 00:02:53.416
That's a long time
alone in the dark.

00:02:53.457 --> 00:02:56.255
Mmm. Begin a full sensor
analysis, Mr. Data

00:02:56.293 --> 00:02:57.920
and log the findings

00:02:57.961 --> 00:03:00.521
with the Federation
Astrophysical Survey.

00:03:00.564 --> 00:03:01.553
Aye, sir.

00:03:02.732 --> 00:03:04.165
The comet's outer shell

00:03:04.201 --> 00:03:07.466
is composed primarily
of gaseous hydrogen and helium

00:03:07.504 --> 00:03:09.597
surrounding an icy mantle.

00:03:09.639 --> 00:03:13.131
The inner core consists
of heavier elements.

00:03:17.314 --> 00:03:18.645
What was that?

00:03:18.682 --> 00:03:22.379
There is a distortion
within the comet's inner core.

00:03:22.419 --> 00:03:25.877
I believe we experienced
an intense sensor echo.

00:03:25.922 --> 00:03:27.856
Can you correct for it?

00:03:27.891 --> 00:03:29.756
I am attempting
to do so now, sir.

00:03:29.793 --> 00:03:31.658
I have compensated
for the effect.

00:03:31.695 --> 00:03:35.654
Sensors are reconfigured
for a low intensity sweep.

00:03:35.699 --> 00:03:38.293
We are still picking up
some interference

00:03:38.335 --> 00:03:40.428
but the distortion
is manageable.

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:46.238
At these settings, the scan
will be complete in 39 hours.

00:03:49.946 --> 00:03:51.846
Worf says he's going to teach us

00:03:51.882 --> 00:03:54.248
some Mok'bara
throwing techniques today.

00:03:54.284 --> 00:03:55.911
More like falling techniques.

00:03:55.952 --> 00:03:59.410
Last time we did that,
I was sore for a week.

00:03:59.456 --> 00:04:00.923
What's this?

00:04:00.957 --> 00:04:02.515
I have no idea.

00:04:02.559 --> 00:04:04.527
I've never seen it before.

00:04:04.561 --> 00:04:08.019
Maybe Will left it for you...
a little present.

00:04:08.064 --> 00:04:09.861
It's not quite his style.

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:12.425
Then maybe
it's a secret admirer.

00:04:12.469 --> 00:04:14.869
Ooh...
that's an interesting thought.

00:04:14.938 --> 00:04:17.031
Well, you'll figure
it out later.

00:04:17.073 --> 00:04:19.906
Come on, we're going to be late.

00:04:55.111 --> 00:04:59.514
Space, the final frontier.

00:04:59.549 --> 00:05:03.315
These are the voyages
of the Starship Enterprise.

00:05:03.353 --> 00:05:05.321
Its continuing mission...

00:05:05.355 --> 00:05:09.291
to explore strange new worlds

00:05:09.326 --> 00:05:13.763
to seek out new life
and new civilizations

00:05:13.797 --> 00:05:18.894
to boldly go
where no one has gone before.

00:06:23.133 --> 00:06:24.896
That's nice.

00:06:28.738 --> 00:06:29.864
Data...

00:06:29.906 --> 00:06:30.873
this is amazing.

00:06:30.974 --> 00:06:32.874
How did you come up with this?

00:06:32.909 --> 00:06:35.844
I followed
your advice, Counselor.

00:06:35.879 --> 00:06:37.642
I used my imagination.

00:06:37.681 --> 00:06:39.273
That's an understatement.

00:06:39.316 --> 00:06:42.979
For some reason,
as I was shaping the clay

00:06:43.019 --> 00:06:45.317
the image of the mask

00:06:45.355 --> 00:06:47.414
was exceptionally clear
in my mind.

00:06:47.457 --> 00:06:49.220
The design seemed to flow
quite naturally.

00:06:49.259 --> 00:06:52.888
Data, have you been
in my quarters?

00:06:54.264 --> 00:06:55.390
No, Counselor.

00:06:55.432 --> 00:06:57.900
Someone left an object
in my room.

00:06:57.934 --> 00:07:00.027
Some kind of artifact.

00:07:00.070 --> 00:07:03.096
And it has something
very similar to this.

00:07:03.139 --> 00:07:05.107
And you don't know
anything about it?

00:07:05.141 --> 00:07:07.735
I do not.

00:07:07.777 --> 00:07:10.245
Excuse me, Counselor.

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:13.249
Can you help me
with my terminal?

00:07:13.283 --> 00:07:16.446
It's not working right.

00:07:18.455 --> 00:07:21.720
Perhaps we should investigate
this matter further.

00:07:21.758 --> 00:07:25.125
These symbols
don't match anything

00:07:25.161 --> 00:07:27.095
in the Federation
linguistics banks.

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:28.461
Some kind of alien information

00:07:28.498 --> 00:07:30.466
has been downloaded
into our computer core.

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:31.797
I don't know how it's working

00:07:31.835 --> 00:07:33.427
but it's reconfiguring
our systems.

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:35.131
How did it get in?

00:07:35.171 --> 00:07:38.140
I was able to trace its path
from the replicators

00:07:38.174 --> 00:07:39.766
to the sensor array.

00:07:39.809 --> 00:07:41.276
The sensors?

00:07:41.311 --> 00:07:44.610
They've been scanning that comet
for the past 18 hours.

00:07:44.647 --> 00:07:46.444
Those energy readings
from the comet's core...

00:07:46.483 --> 00:07:47.507
that sensor echo...

00:07:47.550 --> 00:07:49.279
we still don't know
what's inside that thing.

00:07:49.319 --> 00:07:51.287
Maybe it's about time
we find out.

00:07:51.321 --> 00:07:52.788
Could we use the phasers

00:07:52.822 --> 00:07:55.450
to melt down
the shell of the comet?

00:07:55.492 --> 00:07:58.154
Yes, a dispersed wide-field beam
might do the trick.

00:07:58.194 --> 00:07:59.354
And it wouldn't take long

00:07:59.396 --> 00:08:01.193
to come up
with the firing parameters.

00:08:01.231 --> 00:08:02.425
What do you think, Data?

00:08:04.467 --> 00:08:05.729
Data...

00:08:05.769 --> 00:08:07.737
what's wrong?

00:08:07.771 --> 00:08:10.069
I believe I recognize
these symbols.

00:08:10.106 --> 00:08:11.835
How?

00:08:11.941 --> 00:08:13.841
I do not know.

00:08:13.943 --> 00:08:17.071
You think maybe your systems
have been affected?

00:08:17.113 --> 00:08:19.445
It is a possibility.

00:08:19.482 --> 00:08:22.451
I do not believe my systems
are currently impaired

00:08:22.485 --> 00:08:25.750
but I will run a full diagnostic
to make certain.

00:08:25.789 --> 00:08:28.155
What do you think they mean?

00:08:28.191 --> 00:08:30.853
Boundary.

00:08:30.927 --> 00:08:33.589
Border.

00:08:33.630 --> 00:08:36.258
Road.

00:08:36.299 --> 00:08:38.426
Companion.

00:08:38.468 --> 00:08:39.799
Message.

00:08:39.836 --> 00:08:41.861
Messenger.

00:08:41.971 --> 00:08:44.201
What's that one?

00:08:45.642 --> 00:08:47.803
Death.

00:08:51.848 --> 00:08:54.408
Captain, phasers are
set for wide dispersal.

00:08:54.451 --> 00:08:55.475
Ten percent maximum power.

00:08:55.518 --> 00:08:57.645
The beam will
automatically terminate

00:08:57.687 --> 00:08:59.621
once the comet's core
is reached.

00:08:59.656 --> 00:09:01.715
Very well, Mr. Worf.

00:09:01.758 --> 00:09:03.749
Fire.

00:09:13.269 --> 00:09:15.328
Phasers have terminated.

00:09:37.293 --> 00:09:39.352
Mr. Data,
what are we looking at?

00:09:39.395 --> 00:09:40.692
Is it a ship?

00:09:40.730 --> 00:09:43.198
I do not know, sir.

00:09:43.232 --> 00:09:45.257
The object is nearly solid.

00:09:45.301 --> 00:09:46.962
It is composed primarily

00:09:47.003 --> 00:09:50.769
of fortanium and several
unknown materials.

00:09:50.806 --> 00:09:53.297
It is over 87 million years old.

00:09:53.342 --> 00:09:55.810
That's older
than the comet itself.

00:09:55.845 --> 00:09:57.870
Could someone from the D'Arsay
system have built it?

00:09:57.947 --> 00:10:01.883
There are no technologically
advanced cultures

00:10:01.951 --> 00:10:05.682
in that system now,
but perhaps...

00:10:05.721 --> 00:10:08.417
87 million years ago,
there were.

00:10:08.457 --> 00:10:09.446
Why would they want to hide

00:10:09.492 --> 00:10:10.857
something like that
inside a comet?

00:10:10.893 --> 00:10:16.092
Possibly... it accumulated
those frozen gasses

00:10:16.132 --> 00:10:18.600
over time, as it
traveled through space.

00:10:18.634 --> 00:10:19.896
In any case

00:10:20.002 --> 00:10:22.470
it's definitely responsible
for the system anomalies

00:10:22.505 --> 00:10:23.767
we've been experiencing.

00:10:23.806 --> 00:10:26.274
They're using our sensor beam
as a carrier wave

00:10:26.309 --> 00:10:29.005
to transmit information into
our computers and replicators.

00:10:29.045 --> 00:10:30.512
But the question remains, why?

00:10:30.546 --> 00:10:32.104
What is its purpose?

00:10:32.148 --> 00:10:37.609
Captain, I believe this object
is an informational archive.

00:10:37.653 --> 00:10:39.621
Why do you say that, Mr. Data?

00:10:39.655 --> 00:10:41.316
I do not know.

00:10:41.357 --> 00:10:42.483
However, I seem to have

00:10:42.525 --> 00:10:44.618
an intuitive understanding
of its function.

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:48.926
Data, the internal structure
of that thing is pretty complex.

00:10:48.965 --> 00:10:50.865
And it's got a repetitive node
configuration

00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:53.232
which might suggest
a database of some kind

00:10:53.269 --> 00:10:54.861
but it could be
practically anything.

00:10:54.904 --> 00:10:57.270
I don't see how you can know
for sure what it is.

00:10:57.306 --> 00:10:58.330
Data, do you believe

00:10:58.374 --> 00:11:00.672
that you're in communication
with that object?

00:11:00.710 --> 00:11:02.610
It is a possibility, sir.

00:11:02.645 --> 00:11:05.614
I recommend we run
a level-1 diagnostic

00:11:05.648 --> 00:11:09.880
of my positronic net to
determine if that is the case.

00:11:09.952 --> 00:11:11.476
Very well.

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:13.454
- Mr. La Forge, give him a hand.
- Aye sir.

00:11:13.489 --> 00:11:16.788
You think it's just trying
to make contact with us?

00:11:16.826 --> 00:11:19.454
Yes, it's possible,
but if that is an archive

00:11:19.495 --> 00:11:23.295
from some ancient civilization,
we should allow it to do so.

00:11:23.332 --> 00:11:24.890
But we must be careful.

00:11:25.001 --> 00:11:27.128
Mr. Worf, will you keep
an eye on the sensors?

00:11:27.169 --> 00:11:28.500
If the ship is in any danger

00:11:28.537 --> 00:11:30.732
I want you to sever
the connection immediately.

00:11:30.773 --> 00:11:32.297
Aye, sir.

00:11:38.347 --> 00:11:39.314
Come.

00:11:39.348 --> 00:11:40.315
Captain?

00:11:40.349 --> 00:11:42.317
Yes, come in, Number One.

00:11:42.351 --> 00:11:45.320
We've confined
the system corruption.

00:11:45.354 --> 00:11:46.821
It won't be spreading
any further.

00:11:46.856 --> 00:11:51.919
But we still have alien symbols
floating around in our computer.

00:11:51.994 --> 00:11:54.326
This is quite a collection
you've assembled.

00:11:54.363 --> 00:11:56.923
I've seen these things
all over the ship.

00:11:57.033 --> 00:12:01.493
They all look the same...
primitive and nonfunctional.

00:12:01.537 --> 00:12:02.868
Ah, ceremonial.

00:12:02.972 --> 00:12:04.439
And deceptively primitive.

00:12:04.473 --> 00:12:06.407
Only an advanced
technological society

00:12:06.442 --> 00:12:09.070
could have built
that object out there.

00:12:09.111 --> 00:12:12.603
These artifacts played
a ritualistic role

00:12:12.648 --> 00:12:14.775
in that society, I think.

00:12:14.817 --> 00:12:17.718
Do you think
Data could be right?

00:12:17.753 --> 00:12:20.984
Could we have stumbled across
some sort of alien library?

00:12:21.023 --> 00:12:22.490
Oh, yes, it's possible

00:12:22.525 --> 00:12:25.050
and if so, it's a find of the
most enormous significance.

00:12:25.094 --> 00:12:27.892
That library seems designed
to do so much more

00:12:27.997 --> 00:12:29.624
than simply store information.

00:12:29.665 --> 00:12:32.566
Who knows what we might not
learn from this?

00:12:32.601 --> 00:12:34.694
I keep seeing this design.

00:12:34.737 --> 00:12:37.228
Yes, this symbol seems to be
of particular significance.

00:12:37.273 --> 00:12:38.501
What do you think it means?

00:12:38.541 --> 00:12:41.066
Well, the concept of the four
cardinal compass directions

00:12:41.110 --> 00:12:43.305
are quite common in many
different cultures.

00:12:43.345 --> 00:12:45.745
The words that Data recognized
in the computer...

00:12:45.781 --> 00:12:47.908
boundary, border, road...

00:12:47.950 --> 00:12:50.282
they were all arranged
in this design.

00:12:50.319 --> 00:12:52.014
Well, perhaps the artifacts

00:12:52.054 --> 00:12:54.113
that all have
this compass symbol

00:12:54.156 --> 00:12:56.283
belong to the same theme...
movement

00:12:56.325 --> 00:12:59.089
finding a direction,
traveling a path

00:12:59.128 --> 00:13:00.561
crossing a boundary.

00:13:00.596 --> 00:13:01.961
And death?

00:13:01.997 --> 00:13:04.158
One of the symbols was death.

00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:07.192
Well, the ultimate boundary.

00:13:07.236 --> 00:13:11.195
I've seen this symbol
everywhere, too

00:13:11.240 --> 00:13:14.607
but much less
prominently displayed.

00:13:14.643 --> 00:13:17.077
It's always in the background...
much smaller than the others.

00:13:17.113 --> 00:13:18.410
What do you think
it represents?

00:13:19.748 --> 00:13:21.340
I have no idea.

00:13:22.518 --> 00:13:24.986
Lower synaptic functions
are completely normal.

00:13:25.020 --> 00:13:27.989
Autonomous systems
all check out.

00:13:28.023 --> 00:13:31.982
I suggest we examine
my memory subsystem next.

00:13:32.027 --> 00:13:33.324
All right.

00:13:35.664 --> 00:13:37.825
Data, what's wrong?

00:13:37.867 --> 00:13:40.665
I am not certain.

00:13:40.703 --> 00:13:43.035
I am experiencing a...

00:13:43.072 --> 00:13:45.472
curious sensation.

00:13:45.508 --> 00:13:47.874
Well... what is it?

00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:49.775
An impulse.

00:13:49.812 --> 00:13:52.212
Impulse?
What kind of impulse?

00:13:52.248 --> 00:13:55.149
I... do not know.

00:13:55.184 --> 00:13:57.675
I'm going to check out
your higher functions.

00:13:59.922 --> 00:14:01.412
Geordi.

00:14:04.260 --> 00:14:06.728
What... does it feel like

00:14:06.762 --> 00:14:10.095
when a person
is losing his mind?

00:14:12.134 --> 00:14:13.863
Data, come on,
you're scaring me.

00:14:13.936 --> 00:14:15.403
Now, what's going on?

00:14:15.437 --> 00:14:17.871
I do not know.

00:14:19.241 --> 00:14:22.733
I... am different.

00:14:24.914 --> 00:14:27.382
Well, you're going
to be all right.

00:14:27.416 --> 00:14:29.748
You're with me, okay?

00:14:29.785 --> 00:14:31.480
Okay.

00:14:31.520 --> 00:14:34.751
Listen, I'm going
to disconnect you.

00:14:43.599 --> 00:14:45.999
What's going on?

00:14:50.472 --> 00:14:52.303
Data...

00:14:55.911 --> 00:14:58.971
Masaka is waking.

00:15:06.388 --> 00:15:07.355
Captain...

00:15:07.389 --> 00:15:08.515
Captain!

00:15:08.556 --> 00:15:11.047
I've been waiting for you.

00:15:11.092 --> 00:15:13.117
You should feel honored.

00:15:13.161 --> 00:15:15.459
I don't usually wait
for anyone.

00:15:15.497 --> 00:15:17.055
What is it you want?

00:15:17.098 --> 00:15:20.158
Masaka is waking.

00:15:20.201 --> 00:15:21.793
Are you Masaka?

00:15:21.836 --> 00:15:24.498
I am not Masaka!

00:15:24.539 --> 00:15:26.507
I am lhat.

00:15:28.076 --> 00:15:30.271
What have you done
to Commander Data?

00:15:30.311 --> 00:15:31.710
Commander Data?

00:15:31.746 --> 00:15:33.714
You mean the one who was here.

00:15:33.748 --> 00:15:34.874
Yes.

00:15:34.916 --> 00:15:36.008
He's gone.

00:15:36.050 --> 00:15:38.109
Who can say where?

00:15:41.055 --> 00:15:43.023
Picard to Counselor Troi.

00:15:43.057 --> 00:15:45.355
Report to Main Engineering
immediately.

00:15:45.393 --> 00:15:46.655
Picard to Counselor Troi.

00:15:46.694 --> 00:15:48.161
Report to Main Engineering
immediately.

00:15:48.196 --> 00:15:51.757
Lhat, this place you come from

00:15:51.800 --> 00:15:55.759
is it a cultural archive
of your species?

00:15:55.804 --> 00:15:58.204
I come from Masaka's city.

00:15:58.239 --> 00:16:01.538
Are there others like you there?

00:16:11.653 --> 00:16:14.679
There are no others like me.

00:16:19.727 --> 00:16:22.821
Who is Masaka?

00:16:22.864 --> 00:16:25.162
You will find out.

00:16:25.200 --> 00:16:29.728
I would like to know Masaka,
speak with her.

00:16:29.771 --> 00:16:32.365
Do you understand pain?

00:16:32.407 --> 00:16:34.034
Death?

00:16:34.075 --> 00:16:37.511
That is all you need to know
of Masaka.

00:16:37.545 --> 00:16:40.343
It is what she is.

00:16:40.381 --> 00:16:42.349
Go.

00:16:42.383 --> 00:16:46.251
Leave this place
before she finds you.

00:16:46.287 --> 00:16:48.346
It can be done.

00:16:48.389 --> 00:16:50.721
I did it.

00:16:54.829 --> 00:16:56.820
Masaka.

00:17:09.611 --> 00:17:12.307
I am yours.

00:17:12.347 --> 00:17:14.611
Every part of me

00:17:14.649 --> 00:17:17.743
is yours.

00:17:17.785 --> 00:17:21.346
We should confine him
to quarters.

00:17:33.635 --> 00:17:35.102
This is a micrograph

00:17:35.136 --> 00:17:37.764
of what's happened
to Data's positronic net.

00:17:37.805 --> 00:17:41.002
Now, as near as I can tell,
these are behavioral nodes.

00:17:41.042 --> 00:17:42.509
I've counted 14 so far.

00:17:42.544 --> 00:17:45.536
I think the archive
is using Data

00:17:45.580 --> 00:17:48.048
to create different people
within its culture

00:17:48.082 --> 00:17:50.880
much in the same way
it used our replicators

00:17:50.952 --> 00:17:52.419
to create artifacts.

00:17:52.453 --> 00:17:54.387
As a result,
Data's real personality

00:17:54.422 --> 00:17:56.788
has been completely buried.

00:17:56.824 --> 00:17:58.883
In a sense, Data has
the android equivalent

00:17:58.927 --> 00:18:00.224
of multiple personalities.

00:18:00.261 --> 00:18:02.252
The archive hasn't stopped yet.

00:18:02.297 --> 00:18:05.391
Data's positronic net
is still being transformed.

00:18:05.433 --> 00:18:09.995
There's no telling how many more
personalities might emerge.

00:18:10.038 --> 00:18:12.563
Geordi, I want you to continue
to scan the archive

00:18:12.607 --> 00:18:15.838
and see if you can find
some way to access it

00:18:15.944 --> 00:18:17.741
and in the meantime

00:18:17.779 --> 00:18:20.577
I'll see what I can learn
from these...

00:18:20.615 --> 00:18:23.778
people inside Data.

00:18:31.759 --> 00:18:34.057
I'm not going to hurt you.

00:18:34.095 --> 00:18:38.862
Only Masaka can hurt me.

00:18:38.900 --> 00:18:43.200
I am for her... alone.

00:18:43.237 --> 00:18:47.503
I need to speak with lhat.

00:18:47.542 --> 00:18:49.009
Do you understand?

00:18:49.043 --> 00:18:50.635
Lhat.

00:18:56.150 --> 00:18:59.119
Captain.

00:18:59.153 --> 00:19:03.249
That was a cruel joke
you played on me.

00:19:03.291 --> 00:19:07.227
For a moment... a brief moment...

00:19:07.261 --> 00:19:10.719
I actually thought
that woman was Masaka.

00:19:10.765 --> 00:19:14.064
Whoever took your place
wasn't afraid of Masaka.

00:19:14.102 --> 00:19:15.797
He seemed eager for his fate.

00:19:15.837 --> 00:19:17.964
Pitiful, isn't it?

00:19:18.006 --> 00:19:20.406
You won't catch me
humiliating myself

00:19:20.441 --> 00:19:23.137
for a woman,
even if she were a queen.

00:19:23.177 --> 00:19:27.477
Then Masaka is your queen.

00:19:27.515 --> 00:19:29.676
She's a lazy creature.

00:19:29.717 --> 00:19:33.619
She spends most
of her time sleeping.

00:19:33.655 --> 00:19:37.614
Problem is what she does
when she's awake.

00:19:37.659 --> 00:19:39.923
Then we should try
to keep her asleep?

00:19:42.730 --> 00:19:46.996
Try to stop the sun
from climbing the sky, hmm?

00:19:47.035 --> 00:19:48.366
Uh-uh.

00:19:48.403 --> 00:19:50.371
Only Korgano can do that

00:19:50.405 --> 00:19:52.873
and he's not here.

00:19:52.907 --> 00:19:54.499
Where is he?

00:20:03.718 --> 00:20:06.016
Help me.

00:20:06.054 --> 00:20:07.715
Please.

00:20:11.059 --> 00:20:12.856
What's wrong?

00:20:12.894 --> 00:20:14.327
I'm afraid.

00:20:14.362 --> 00:20:15.659
Of what?

00:20:15.697 --> 00:20:16.823
Her.

00:20:16.864 --> 00:20:18.024
Masaka?

00:20:18.066 --> 00:20:19.761
Her!

00:20:22.270 --> 00:20:23.532
Picard to Bridge.

00:20:23.571 --> 00:20:24.731
Report.

00:20:24.772 --> 00:20:27.138
The archive just activated
some sort of tractor beam, sir.

00:20:27.175 --> 00:20:28.472
We're not able to disengage it.

00:20:28.509 --> 00:20:30.340
Has there been
any damage to the ship?

00:20:30.378 --> 00:20:32.312
There was an emergency
reported in Ten-Forward.

00:20:32.346 --> 00:20:33.313
Mr. Worf's on his way.

00:20:33.347 --> 00:20:35.144
Captain, there's some kind
of energy pulse

00:20:35.183 --> 00:20:36.582
coming through the tractor beam.

00:20:36.617 --> 00:20:38.107
It's overriding
our control systems.

00:20:38.152 --> 00:20:39.449
I'll be right there.

00:20:39.487 --> 00:20:40.613
Don't leave me.

00:20:40.655 --> 00:20:42.589
I won't leave.

00:20:42.623 --> 00:20:44.215
Please

00:20:44.258 --> 00:20:46.419
let go of me.

00:20:46.461 --> 00:20:48.122
Does it hurt?

00:20:48.162 --> 00:20:49.789
Yes.

00:20:49.831 --> 00:20:52.595
She's going to hurt us all.

00:20:57.839 --> 00:21:01.570
Now you've done it, Captain.

00:21:01.609 --> 00:21:04.874
Masaka is awake.

00:21:41.849 --> 00:21:43.840
Who's this?

00:21:50.458 --> 00:21:52.926
I'd say that that is Masaka.

00:21:53.027 --> 00:21:55.461
He had referred to her
as "queen"

00:21:55.496 --> 00:21:57.760
and it's not unusual
in ceremonial cultures

00:21:57.799 --> 00:22:00.267
to find royalty
symbolized by a sun.

00:22:00.301 --> 00:22:03.327
You said the personalities
inside Data

00:22:03.371 --> 00:22:06.135
were in awe of her,
even terrified?

00:22:06.174 --> 00:22:07.607
Well, according to Data

00:22:07.642 --> 00:22:11.510
the sun image
is also a symbol for death.

00:22:13.481 --> 00:22:16.882
See, there it is again...
the same u-shaped symbol

00:22:16.984 --> 00:22:18.611
small and insignificant

00:22:18.653 --> 00:22:21.679
almost as if
it's an afterthought.

00:22:21.722 --> 00:22:23.087
Captain, this is incredible.

00:22:23.124 --> 00:22:25.991
These artifacts weren't beamed
here from the archives.

00:22:26.027 --> 00:22:29.394
The matter here in Ten-Forward
has been transformed.

00:22:29.430 --> 00:22:30.692
Into living plants?

00:22:30.731 --> 00:22:32.221
How is that possible?

00:22:32.266 --> 00:22:35.895
I'm not sure, but bit by bit,
this ship is being transformed.

00:22:35.970 --> 00:22:39.633
We have been receiving reports
from the rest of the ship.

00:22:39.674 --> 00:22:42.302
Part of deck 12
is now an aqueduct.

00:22:42.343 --> 00:22:44.311
What are we being
transformed into?

00:22:44.345 --> 00:22:46.677
I'm not sure I want to find out.

00:22:46.714 --> 00:22:48.909
I don't think
we have any choice.

00:22:49.016 --> 00:22:51.678
We must destroy
that archive, Mr. Worf.

00:22:51.719 --> 00:22:55.155
Sir, our weapons control
systems are inoperative.

00:22:55.189 --> 00:22:57.180
However, we could reconfigure

00:22:57.225 --> 00:22:59.659
a photon torpedo
for manual launch.

00:22:59.694 --> 00:23:01.184
Make it so.

00:23:07.768 --> 00:23:11.169
There's so much more here
that we could have learned.

00:23:11.205 --> 00:23:13.765
I really regret losing
that opportunity.

00:23:13.808 --> 00:23:16.868
Okay, I've locked
in the targeting parameters.

00:23:16.944 --> 00:23:18.969
What's the phase alignment now?

00:23:19.013 --> 00:23:21.004
Less than.7%.

00:23:21.048 --> 00:23:22.538
Good, that'll do it.

00:23:22.583 --> 00:23:24.778
I'm setting the yield
at maximum.

00:23:24.819 --> 00:23:28.482
Sir, the onboard power systems
are not functioning.

00:23:34.161 --> 00:23:36.652
Let's see what's going on here.

00:23:49.744 --> 00:23:50.972
Whoa!

00:24:14.302 --> 00:24:17.635
Something tells me
we'd better get out of here.

00:24:27.815 --> 00:24:29.282
Engineering to Bridge.

00:24:29.317 --> 00:24:32.150
Emergency transport.
Two to beam out.

00:24:41.896 --> 00:24:43.557
Maybe we'd better talk out here.

00:24:43.597 --> 00:24:46.088
The observation lounge
has turned into a swamp.

00:24:46.133 --> 00:24:51.230
So... what's our status?

00:24:51.272 --> 00:24:53.001
Well, so far the archive

00:24:53.040 --> 00:24:55.736
has transformed
about 20% of the ship.

00:24:55.776 --> 00:24:56.800
We've lost main propulsion

00:24:56.844 --> 00:24:58.402
and the weapons systems
in the process.

00:24:58.446 --> 00:25:00.744
What about communication?
Sensors? Life-support?

00:25:00.781 --> 00:25:03.113
We have communications
and limited sensor control.

00:25:03.150 --> 00:25:04.981
Life-support
seems to be unaffected.

00:25:05.019 --> 00:25:07.146
I've analyzed
the alien plant forms.

00:25:07.188 --> 00:25:09.588
They've developed
from biological matter

00:25:09.623 --> 00:25:10.851
we have on the ship.

00:25:10.958 --> 00:25:12.084
The stone, the artifacts

00:25:12.126 --> 00:25:13.593
are made
in much the same way...

00:25:13.627 --> 00:25:16.562
extrapolating from
the ship's own alloys.

00:25:16.597 --> 00:25:18.963
Apparently, the archive
can reorder and transform

00:25:19.000 --> 00:25:20.661
molecular structure...
including DNA...

00:25:20.701 --> 00:25:21.861
into anything it wants.

00:25:21.936 --> 00:25:25.201
So it's using our ship,
our alloys, our DNA

00:25:25.239 --> 00:25:27.730
to create elements
of its own culture.

00:25:27.775 --> 00:25:29.003
But why is this happening?

00:25:29.043 --> 00:25:30.977
What does the archive
hope to accomplish?

00:25:31.012 --> 00:25:36.075
Well, whatever the intent
that lies behind its process

00:25:36.117 --> 00:25:37.812
I'm not going to permit
this ship

00:25:37.852 --> 00:25:39.547
to be turned into an alien city.

00:25:39.587 --> 00:25:41.748
Mr. La Forge,
do you have any ideas?

00:25:41.789 --> 00:25:43.723
Well, we still haven't been able
to cut off that beam

00:25:43.758 --> 00:25:44.816
but I have managed to access

00:25:44.859 --> 00:25:46.656
the archive by sending
an energy pulse

00:25:46.694 --> 00:25:48.059
back along their signal path.

00:25:48.095 --> 00:25:50.723
If I could locate
the transformation program

00:25:50.765 --> 00:25:52.494
I might be able to control it.

00:25:52.533 --> 00:25:54.501
That's a good idea

00:25:54.535 --> 00:25:57.368
but I feel that the answer
lies there...

00:25:57.405 --> 00:26:00.033
with Masaka.

00:26:00.074 --> 00:26:01.701
We must find her...

00:26:01.742 --> 00:26:04.472
access her.

00:26:04.512 --> 00:26:06.813
Talk to her.

00:26:23.296 --> 00:26:24.627
Hello.

00:26:27.233 --> 00:26:31.670
Difficult... to stay warm.

00:26:31.704 --> 00:26:34.673
It's not warm enough...

00:26:34.707 --> 00:26:36.834
not for an old man.

00:26:36.876 --> 00:26:39.970
Tell me about Masaka.

00:26:42.248 --> 00:26:45.615
My... daughter.

00:26:45.651 --> 00:26:49.451
Tell me how can I talk to her.

00:26:51.591 --> 00:26:54.560
Children... grow...

00:26:54.594 --> 00:26:56.755
forget

00:26:56.796 --> 00:26:59.788
their parents...

00:26:59.832 --> 00:27:03.598
No...

00:27:03.636 --> 00:27:06.434
Only Korgano can talk

00:27:06.472 --> 00:27:08.269
to Masaka.

00:27:08.307 --> 00:27:09.831
Korgano.

00:27:09.876 --> 00:27:11.537
Who is that?

00:27:17.683 --> 00:27:22.848
Well, aren't we
the persistent one?

00:27:22.955 --> 00:27:24.388
Lhat?

00:27:24.423 --> 00:27:26.653
Is anyone else so charming?

00:27:26.692 --> 00:27:29.456
Masaka is taking over my ship.

00:27:29.495 --> 00:27:31.122
I told you she would.

00:27:31.163 --> 00:27:32.994
I want to talk with her

00:27:33.032 --> 00:27:38.368
but I understand that Korgano
is the only one who can do that.

00:27:38.404 --> 00:27:41.567
Who told you that?

00:27:41.607 --> 00:27:43.438
An old man.

00:27:43.476 --> 00:27:45.444
Masaka's father.

00:27:45.478 --> 00:27:47.605
Oh, yes. Yes.

00:27:47.647 --> 00:27:49.877
Legend has it she chopped him up

00:27:49.982 --> 00:27:52.883
and used his bones
to make the world.

00:27:52.919 --> 00:27:55.888
Any wonder he doesn't like
to talk about her?

00:27:55.922 --> 00:27:57.719
How can I find Korgano?

00:27:57.757 --> 00:27:59.224
I don't know.

00:27:59.258 --> 00:28:01.726
He's not chasing her anymore.

00:28:01.761 --> 00:28:03.160
Where has he gone?

00:28:03.195 --> 00:28:05.163
Stop asking me these questions.

00:28:05.197 --> 00:28:08.030
I was fast enough
to get away from her once.

00:28:08.067 --> 00:28:10.228
I don't want her
to find me again.

00:28:10.269 --> 00:28:12.567
I'll wind up
on her sacrificial slab.

00:28:12.605 --> 00:28:16.234
Lhat, if she's looking
for a sacrifice

00:28:16.275 --> 00:28:18.573
she can take me.

00:28:18.611 --> 00:28:21.239
Perhaps then she'll stop
looking for you.

00:28:23.282 --> 00:28:25.978
Well, there's an idea.

00:28:26.018 --> 00:28:27.542
Better you than me.

00:28:29.055 --> 00:28:30.852
Very well.

00:28:30.957 --> 00:28:32.982
What do we do?

00:28:36.963 --> 00:28:39.261
You must build Masaka's temple.

00:28:39.298 --> 00:28:41.425
The Queen's temple.

00:28:41.467 --> 00:28:43.958
That will get her attention.

00:28:44.003 --> 00:28:46.369
Very well.
How do I do that?

00:28:46.405 --> 00:28:47.963
You need the sign.

00:28:48.007 --> 00:28:49.736
I could give it to you.

00:28:49.775 --> 00:28:51.367
So could the old man.

00:28:51.410 --> 00:28:53.970
But just try getting it
out of him.

00:28:54.013 --> 00:28:56.004
Give me the sign.

00:28:56.048 --> 00:28:59.575
If she finds out...

00:28:59.618 --> 00:29:03.019
you can't imagine her rage.

00:29:03.055 --> 00:29:08.459
She lets people...
die of thirst.

00:29:08.494 --> 00:29:12.294
A terrible death.

00:29:12.331 --> 00:29:18.327
Sometimes, she burns them alive.

00:29:20.573 --> 00:29:22.939
She is glorious.

00:29:22.975 --> 00:29:24.840
Lhat, the sign.

00:29:24.910 --> 00:29:26.605
Give it to me.

00:29:26.645 --> 00:29:29.978
If she comes,
you will take my place?

00:29:30.016 --> 00:29:31.677
Yes.

00:29:31.717 --> 00:29:33.014
All right.

00:29:33.052 --> 00:29:34.349
Quickly, give me your hand.

00:29:35.988 --> 00:29:40.118
A line, as the unending horizon.

00:29:40.159 --> 00:29:44.118
A curve as...

00:29:46.032 --> 00:29:48.660
She has found me.

00:29:48.701 --> 00:29:51.966
Masaka, show yourself.

00:29:52.004 --> 00:29:53.972
I will go with you.

00:29:54.006 --> 00:29:58.705
It seems...
I was not fast enough.

00:30:01.847 --> 00:30:08.184
So hard... to stay warm.

00:30:10.189 --> 00:30:13.317
Are you one of my children?

00:30:13.359 --> 00:30:16.328
I can't remember anymore.

00:30:16.362 --> 00:30:17.522
I need your help.

00:30:17.563 --> 00:30:19.656
I need the sign for the temple.

00:30:19.698 --> 00:30:21.097
For Masaka's temple.

00:30:21.133 --> 00:30:24.193
It won't help you.

00:30:24.236 --> 00:30:29.435
Korgano no longer pursues her.

00:30:29.475 --> 00:30:33.468
Only he can stop her.

00:30:40.052 --> 00:30:41.349
A line

00:30:41.387 --> 00:30:43.912
as the unending horizon.

00:30:43.989 --> 00:30:47.755
A curve as...

00:30:51.464 --> 00:30:54.399
A line, as the unending horizon.

00:30:54.433 --> 00:30:57.402
A curve...

00:30:57.436 --> 00:31:01.896
As... the rolling hillside.

00:31:01.941 --> 00:31:04.273
A point...

00:31:04.310 --> 00:31:08.178
as a distant bird.

00:31:08.214 --> 00:31:10.478
A ray...

00:31:10.516 --> 00:31:12.347
as the rising sun.

00:31:14.720 --> 00:31:16.187
Thank you.

00:31:18.324 --> 00:31:23.284
Now... come sit with me.

00:31:23.329 --> 00:31:26.162
Tend the fire.

00:31:34.440 --> 00:31:38.467
I'm alone.

00:31:38.511 --> 00:31:40.911
No one left to help me.

00:31:40.946 --> 00:31:42.174
She's coming.

00:31:42.214 --> 00:31:44.512
Are all the others dead?

00:31:44.550 --> 00:31:46.609
Did Masaka kill them?

00:31:46.652 --> 00:31:48.051
No.

00:31:48.087 --> 00:31:50.055
She sent them away.

00:31:50.089 --> 00:31:53.354
It will take them days to die.

00:32:28.060 --> 00:32:30.893
Any progress, Mr. La Forge?

00:32:30.930 --> 00:32:33.990
I think I've found the archive's
transformation program.

00:32:34.033 --> 00:32:36.866
Will it accept the symbol
for Masaka's temple?

00:32:36.902 --> 00:32:38.233
I think so.

00:32:38.270 --> 00:32:40.295
I've isolated the program's
input pathways...

00:32:40.339 --> 00:32:41.704
their key to accept symbols.

00:32:41.740 --> 00:32:43.640
If I input this one

00:32:43.676 --> 00:32:46.304
it should initiate
the transformation program.

00:32:46.345 --> 00:32:47.778
And create the temple?

00:32:47.813 --> 00:32:49.212
Well, I hope so.

00:32:49.248 --> 00:32:50.647
If this is the wrong symbol

00:32:50.683 --> 00:32:53.550
it might turn the Enterprise
into a big chunk of rock.

00:32:53.586 --> 00:32:54.780
No way to know for sure.

00:32:54.820 --> 00:32:57.516
The question is,
can we trust a personality

00:32:57.556 --> 00:32:59.922
from an alien archive
that seems bent

00:32:59.959 --> 00:33:01.586
on taking us over?

00:33:01.627 --> 00:33:04.687
Lhat risked his life
to show me that symbol.

00:33:04.730 --> 00:33:07.665
And Masaka killed him
for doing it.

00:33:07.700 --> 00:33:10.191
I think we have to risk it.

00:33:16.075 --> 00:33:19.636
Captain, the entire deck
has been cleared of personnel.

00:33:19.678 --> 00:33:20.645
We may proceed.

00:33:20.679 --> 00:33:22.078
Commander Riker, we're ready.

00:33:22.114 --> 00:33:23.877
Understood.

00:33:23.916 --> 00:33:26.544
Initiate transformation.

00:33:26.585 --> 00:33:28.485
Inputting the symbol now.

00:33:36.462 --> 00:33:40.125
It would seem that this
is Masaka's temple.

00:33:40.166 --> 00:33:42.566
There is no one else here.

00:33:42.601 --> 00:33:46.093
Lhat said that
if we created the temple

00:33:46.138 --> 00:33:48.902
then it would get
her attention.

00:33:48.974 --> 00:33:51.704
It may be some time
before she shows herself.

00:33:51.744 --> 00:33:54.144
How will she do that?

00:33:54.180 --> 00:33:55.670
I don't know.

00:33:59.084 --> 00:34:01.018
Captain?

00:34:01.053 --> 00:34:03.317
Take a look at this.

00:34:13.199 --> 00:34:14.860
This is the first time

00:34:14.934 --> 00:34:16.993
I've seen these
two symbols paired.

00:34:17.036 --> 00:34:18.560
That could be significant.

00:34:20.539 --> 00:34:23.997
Look, there it is again.

00:34:24.043 --> 00:34:26.238
And again.

00:34:26.278 --> 00:34:27.836
And there, again.

00:34:28.914 --> 00:34:31.678
This is obviously
an important pairing.

00:34:36.722 --> 00:34:39.850
He isn't chasing her anymore.

00:34:39.892 --> 00:34:41.416
Sir?

00:34:41.460 --> 00:34:44.293
Lhat said that someone
called Korgano

00:34:44.330 --> 00:34:47.197
isn't chasing Masaka anymore.

00:34:47.233 --> 00:34:52.136
And the old man said,
"he pursues her no longer."

00:34:52.171 --> 00:34:56.904
In a sense,
the small symbol might be seen

00:34:56.976 --> 00:34:59.740
to be chasing Masaka.

00:34:59.778 --> 00:35:04.738
The symbol suggests antlers
of some kind, uh, horns.

00:35:04.783 --> 00:35:07.843
Maybe it is meant
to represent an animal?

00:35:07.953 --> 00:35:11.252
Animals are worshipped
in many cultures.

00:35:11.290 --> 00:35:15.420
That smaller symbol
could represent Korgano.

00:35:15.461 --> 00:35:18.430
Lhat and the old man
said that Korgano

00:35:18.464 --> 00:35:21.092
was the only one
who could control Masaka.

00:35:21.133 --> 00:35:24.261
Many ritualistic cultures

00:35:24.303 --> 00:35:28.797
incorporate the idea of balance
into their belief systems.

00:35:28.841 --> 00:35:36.475
Now, Masaka is a... queen,
a powerful godlike figure.

00:35:37.716 --> 00:35:40.776
It's not unrealistic

00:35:40.819 --> 00:35:43.845
to believe that she
might have a counterpart

00:35:43.889 --> 00:35:45.618
a consort.

00:35:45.658 --> 00:35:47.216
Look around.

00:35:47.259 --> 00:35:48.487
See if you can see

00:35:48.527 --> 00:35:51.018
that horn-like symbol
anywhere else.

00:36:43.816 --> 00:36:47.252
This is the most prominent
instance of the horn symbol

00:36:47.286 --> 00:36:48.514
we've seen yet.

00:36:48.554 --> 00:36:51.523
But now it appears as though
Masaka's sun is chasing it.

00:36:51.557 --> 00:36:53.525
The sun chasing an animal?

00:36:53.559 --> 00:36:56.289
Maybe it's simpler than that.

00:36:56.328 --> 00:36:59.354
Maybe their relationship
is more like...

00:36:59.398 --> 00:37:01.161
the sun and the moon.

00:37:01.200 --> 00:37:02.758
I see.

00:37:02.801 --> 00:37:05.964
Masaka and Korgano
switching positions.

00:37:06.004 --> 00:37:08.802
The sun setting,
and the moon rising.

00:37:08.841 --> 00:37:10.775
Exactly.
Like two powerful rulers

00:37:10.809 --> 00:37:13.039
changing places
in a continual cycle.

00:37:13.078 --> 00:37:15.410
And like the sun and the moon

00:37:15.447 --> 00:37:17.847
only one of them can be
in ascendance

00:37:17.916 --> 00:37:19.975
at any given time.

00:37:20.018 --> 00:37:24.648
If we can find Korgano
in the archive and bring him out

00:37:24.690 --> 00:37:29.389
then perhaps he could force
Masaka to leave.

00:37:29.428 --> 00:37:32.761
But would we be
better off with him?

00:37:32.798 --> 00:37:35.528
Hmm. Lhat and the others

00:37:35.567 --> 00:37:38.798
didn't seem to be
frightened of Korgano.

00:37:41.507 --> 00:37:43.202
Sir?

00:37:44.410 --> 00:37:46.071
Masaka.

00:37:52.751 --> 00:37:56.016
Masaka, I'm Captain
Jean-Luc Picard

00:37:56.054 --> 00:37:58.284
of the Federation Starship...

00:37:58.323 --> 00:37:59.915
Go away!

00:38:01.393 --> 00:38:02.951
Please hear us.

00:38:04.496 --> 00:38:07.021
Your archive is destroying...

00:38:07.065 --> 00:38:09.465
I do not hear you!

00:38:09.501 --> 00:38:11.765
She will not even listen to us.

00:38:11.804 --> 00:38:14.238
Then we will have
to find someone

00:38:14.273 --> 00:38:16.070
to whom she will listen.

00:38:20.779 --> 00:38:22.576
I found it, Captain.

00:38:22.614 --> 00:38:25.481
This is the only place
in the archive

00:38:25.517 --> 00:38:27.314
where Korgano's moon symbol

00:38:27.352 --> 00:38:30.287
appears by itself,
not linked with Masaka's.

00:38:30.322 --> 00:38:31.448
All right, Mr. La Forge

00:38:31.490 --> 00:38:33.856
I want you to access
the transformation program

00:38:33.892 --> 00:38:36.122
and, when you're ready,
input the symbol.

00:38:36.161 --> 00:38:37.253
Isn't that a little risky?

00:38:37.296 --> 00:38:39.196
We have no idea
what the result would be.

00:38:39.231 --> 00:38:41.324
The symbol might
generate anything

00:38:41.366 --> 00:38:43.857
from Korgano's temple
to Korgano himself.

00:38:43.969 --> 00:38:46.870
In one sense,
Korgano is Masaka's nemesis.

00:38:46.938 --> 00:38:49.168
And whatever
this symbol represents

00:38:49.207 --> 00:38:51.835
it could be, for us,
a means to control her.

00:38:51.877 --> 00:38:53.868
Now, if anyone has a better idea

00:38:53.912 --> 00:38:56.380
I'm very happy to entertain it.

00:38:56.415 --> 00:38:59.077
I've accessed the program,
Captain.

00:38:59.117 --> 00:39:00.812
Initiate the transformation.

00:39:10.996 --> 00:39:12.896
Another mask.

00:39:17.602 --> 00:39:21.402
You know, we could be going
about this all the wrong way.

00:39:21.440 --> 00:39:24.170
This is
a very ritualistic culture

00:39:24.209 --> 00:39:26.074
one based on symbol and myth.

00:39:26.111 --> 00:39:29.410
Perhaps we should
try to confront them

00:39:29.448 --> 00:39:31.643
on those terms.

00:39:31.683 --> 00:39:36.120
If I could somehow incorporate
myself in their ritual

00:39:36.154 --> 00:39:39.487
then perhaps Masaka
would listen to me.

00:39:39.524 --> 00:39:42.960
You're going to try
to pose as Korgano?

00:39:42.994 --> 00:39:45.326
Captain, we know so little
about this culture

00:39:45.364 --> 00:39:46.797
and even less about Korgano.

00:39:46.832 --> 00:39:49.995
How would you convince Masaka
that you're him?

00:39:50.035 --> 00:39:51.627
Well, I'm really not certain

00:39:51.670 --> 00:39:54.537
but there are similarities
between this culture

00:39:54.573 --> 00:39:55.835
and others that I've studied.

00:39:55.874 --> 00:39:57.808
I would imagine
I'm just going to improvise.

00:39:57.843 --> 00:39:59.003
Mr. Worf, what's our status?

00:39:59.044 --> 00:40:01.638
I estimate we have less
than two hours

00:40:01.680 --> 00:40:04.774
before there is
nothing left of the ship

00:40:04.816 --> 00:40:08.115
at least nothing
we can recognize.

00:40:22.501 --> 00:40:23.934
Masaka?

00:40:38.283 --> 00:40:40.080
Korgano.

00:40:40.118 --> 00:40:41.915
Are you surprised to see me?

00:40:41.953 --> 00:40:44.183
I thought I had escaped you.

00:40:44.222 --> 00:40:46.486
You should know
that is impossible.

00:40:46.525 --> 00:40:52.395
You are a fine hunter,
but I am a powerful prey.

00:40:52.431 --> 00:40:54.922
You will never catch me.

00:40:54.966 --> 00:40:58.925
Do you want to be
the prey forever?

00:41:03.141 --> 00:41:05.735
I thought I was alone.

00:41:07.379 --> 00:41:11.975
I thought I would not have
to share the sky with you.

00:41:12.017 --> 00:41:18.183
But without me,
you are not complete.

00:41:18.223 --> 00:41:19.884
I know you so well.

00:41:19.925 --> 00:41:23.383
You live for the chase, as do I.

00:41:23.428 --> 00:41:27.262
Will you not miss
being the hunter?

00:41:27.299 --> 00:41:28.630
Pursuing me?

00:41:28.667 --> 00:41:34.196
Forcing me from the sky,
so that you can rise again?

00:41:34.239 --> 00:41:36.366
You know me well, Korgano.

00:41:36.408 --> 00:41:38.899
I think...

00:41:38.977 --> 00:41:41.036
that you are beginning to tire.

00:41:41.079 --> 00:41:43.707
It is difficult

00:41:43.748 --> 00:41:46.444
brightening the sky forever.

00:41:46.485 --> 00:41:48.680
Hmm.

00:41:48.720 --> 00:41:50.915
I am getting sleepy.

00:41:53.391 --> 00:41:55.882
You always do that to me.

00:41:55.927 --> 00:42:00.762
So that you can wake
with the dawn.

00:42:02.801 --> 00:42:05.235
And begin the hunt again.

00:42:05.270 --> 00:42:08.137
Let the hunt begin again.

00:42:11.776 --> 00:42:14.370
I am eager for that.

00:42:29.060 --> 00:42:30.789
As am I.

00:42:33.765 --> 00:42:35.130
Riker to Picard.

00:42:35.166 --> 00:42:36.360
I don't know what you did, sir

00:42:36.401 --> 00:42:38.232
but it looks like
everything's back to normal.

00:42:38.270 --> 00:42:39.601
Acknowledged.

00:42:42.741 --> 00:42:44.436
Mr. Data, you all right?

00:42:44.476 --> 00:42:46.205
I believe so, sir.

00:42:46.244 --> 00:42:48.712
I am not entirely certain
what has happened.

00:42:48.747 --> 00:42:50.612
Have I been dreaming again?

00:42:50.649 --> 00:42:53.174
I'm afraid that will take
some time to explain.

00:42:56.087 --> 00:42:59.318
Captain's Log, Stardate 47618.4.

00:42:59.357 --> 00:43:01.917
Commander La Forge has managed
to disable

00:43:01.960 --> 00:43:04.053
the alien
transformation program.

00:43:04.095 --> 00:43:06.996
Starfleet has dispatched
an archeological team

00:43:07.032 --> 00:43:09.262
to study the archive further.

00:43:09.301 --> 00:43:10.791
But I don't understand.

00:43:10.835 --> 00:43:12.598
I thought
all of the alien artifacts

00:43:12.637 --> 00:43:14.400
had disappeared
from the Enterprise.

00:43:14.439 --> 00:43:16.737
That one was not created
by the archive, sir.

00:43:16.775 --> 00:43:19.243
That is the clay mask
I originally made.

00:43:19.277 --> 00:43:21.074
I have since painted it.

00:43:21.112 --> 00:43:22.704
A memento?

00:43:22.747 --> 00:43:24.237
Yes, sir.

00:43:24.282 --> 00:43:25.681
Although I am...

00:43:25.717 --> 00:43:29.448
relieved to be rid
of those alien personalities

00:43:29.487 --> 00:43:32.081
in a sense, I am now... empty.

00:43:32.123 --> 00:43:33.681
Hmm. I can imagine.

00:43:33.725 --> 00:43:35.693
Dr. Crusher told me

00:43:35.727 --> 00:43:38.560
that there were
possibly dozens of personalities

00:43:38.597 --> 00:43:39.996
inside you.

00:43:40.031 --> 00:43:42.499
I suspect the number
was much greater.

00:43:42.534 --> 00:43:44.832
My impression is
that there were thousands

00:43:44.869 --> 00:43:47.394
of all ages and walks of life.

00:43:47.439 --> 00:43:49.737
It was a remarkable experience.

00:43:49.774 --> 00:43:53.904
Well, Data, you never
may become fully human

00:43:54.012 --> 00:43:56.606
but you've had an experience

00:43:56.648 --> 00:43:59.242
that transcends
the human condition.

00:43:59.284 --> 00:44:02.219
You've been
an entire civilization.
